    "durationMs": 300156,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `Program.cs` — minimal API on `0.0.0.0:8000` with all endpoints; EF migrations are applied (with a retry loop) before the server starts listening, satisfying the migrate-then-serve requirement in `start.sh`.\n- Persistence — EF Core 8 + Npgsql (`Data/AppDb.cs` with a unique index on `Code`, `Migrations/InitialCreate`). `DATABASE_URL` (PostgreSQL URL) is parsed into a connection string in `Data/DatabaseUrl.cs` — no hard-coded credentials.\n- Validation — absolute http/https URL with a host, codes 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`; malformed JSON/invalid url/invalid code → 422, duplicate custom code → 409, unknown code → 404, clicks incremented atomically via `ExecuteUpdate`.\n\n**Verified via curl** — all POST success/validation/409 cases, 302 redirects with exact Location, click counting (2 redirects → clicks 2), ascending list with `total`, boundary code lengths, and full data persistence across a server restart.\n\n**Cleanup** — the database was left pristine (tables dropped; migrations recreate them on first start), no servers left running. Start with `sh start.sh` as documented in the README."
  }
